{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1332240-technocracy-how-do-truly-powerful-technocrats-look-like","id":1332240,"title":"Technocracy: How do truly powerful technocrats look like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-22T23:40:09-07:00","id":1332240,"title":"Technocracy: How do truly powerful technocrats look like?","content":"So back on that idea of PJO and M: TA crossover, I'm thinking of porting over an almagam of high level technocrats. Lowest is Arete 5, highest is Arete 7. Augustine Aleph is one of them. All from different Conventions. <br /> <br /> So here's the thing. August Aleph is Arete 7. He has permanent procedures that alter perception, history, and reality such that he is always perceived to be the second highest authority to any military, letting him walk in and out of the most secretive installations and use their assets to destroy enemies of the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> Are there any guidelines to make truly powerful mages, and not just that, Technocrats? Technocrats usually need to go around with the trappings of the modern world, so I'm not too sure on how to write them in that doesn't just make them seem like Ubermage#19381.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T07:42:24-07:00","id":1332282,"title":"","content":"Note that the Technocracy didn't get where they are today through overwhelming power. They got where they are today through overwhelming leverage. They play to their strengths. They look for unprotected weak points where they can undermine belief in other paradigms or shore up belief in their own. You can write them so that they don't seem like ubermages by focusing on the utility of their effects rather than the power. The ability to just move in and out of military installations is a good one in that regard. It is both broader and more specific than it has to be, though. It is so much world alteration for such a narrow application. <br /> <br /> I'd actually say it should be split into two effects, a permanent &quot;always look like you are supposed to be there&quot; and an optional &quot;insert a proper backstory into all nearby computer systems.&quot; The first one can be a mental effect based on psychological principles, the second one a semi-sentient AI program.<br /> <br /> Or if you wanted to make it less about August's personal power, keep the AI/computer effect, but change the permanent perception effect into a Paradox effect he can't shut off. Something like: people have an exceptionally hard time perceiving or remembering anything out of the ordinary about him. For instance, he could punch someone in the face and they would have to roll willpower or they'd think they just had a headache. The downside is no one can remember instructions or orders he gives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T22:41:43-07:00","id":1332420,"title":"","content":"Outside of super cyborgs I guess the 'strongest Technocrats' are just the guys who showed up, hit a button, and nuked the fuck out of Ravnos and then slapped him with a space laser.<br /> <br /> I guess being a high ranking Technocrat = Access to the space laser gun.<br /> <br /> However keep in mind the Technocracy believe/have information on psychics, so a powerful Technocrat thats a psychic...is basically a reality deviant in the shit they can do. Make people explode, levitate stuff, mind control, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T22:49:55-07:00","id":1332421,"title":"","content":"They look like the cigarette smoking man","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T00:37:19-07:00","id":1332424,"title":"","content":"Some ideas<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Kq89hBdoXlU\" data-code=\"Kq89hBdoXlU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Kq89hBdoXlU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=elMikUGFfqw\" data-code=\"elMikUGFfqw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/elMikUGFfqw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CZc3gSGf23k\" data-code=\"CZc3gSGf23k\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/CZc3gSGf23k/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-24-2019, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-25T12:05:20-07:00","id":1332557,"title":"","content":"JC Denton towards the end of Deus Ex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T05:09:30-07:00","id":1332636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1332240-technocracy-how-do-truly-powerful-technocrats-look-like?p=1332424#post1332424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some ideas</div> </div> </div> </div>The first minute of the first video it's like they were talking about the Week of Nigthmares <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T10:12:00-07:00","id":1332667,"title":"","content":"I don't really know what PJO refers to, so I don't know how helpful my answer will be.^^<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with really powerful mages can be that they, for the most part, do not reside in the normal world anymore, but stay in umbra constructs. To the extend that it is even difficult for them to visit the normal world any longer because of permaparadox.<br /> Also, and this is probably even more so the case for Technocrats, they are the guys in the background. A powerful technocrat using a high level Forces spell for example looks a lot like someone authorizing a nuclear launch.<br /> <br /> The Deus Ex video clip above is a very good example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T07:13:48-07:00","id":1333525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1332240-technocracy-how-do-truly-powerful-technocrats-look-like?p=1332667#post1332667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really know what PJO refers to, so I don't know how helpful my answer will be.^^<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with really powerful mages can be that they, for the most part, do not reside in the normal world anymore, but stay in umbra constructs. To the extend that it is even difficult for them to visit the normal world any longer because of permaparadox.<br /> Also, and this is probably even more so the case for Technocrats, they are the guys in the background. A powerful technocrat using a high level Forces spell for example looks a lot like someone authorizing a nuclear launch.<br /> <br /> The Deus Ex video clip above is a very good example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pjo is Percy Jackson.<br /> <br /> In other words, powerful technocrats are the might of the modern world, distilled and perfected to godlike levels. Just as a caveman would view airstrikes, cars, computers, and the internet as sorcery, so so modern humans view high powered technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T06:23:44-07:00","id":1333660,"title":"","content":"Kind of, in the sense that Technology in M:tA is Magic. The difference being that certain forms of Magic technologies have been accepted my the masses as basically \u201cstuff that should work under the laws of reality\u201d. So one Mage shooting a fireball from his staff an another launching a a rocket from a rocket launcher, both are forms of Magic they just use different Tools. And one is accepted by ordinary people as \u201cstuff that should work\u201c while the other is seen as \u201cstuff that shouldn't work. In the Dark Ages the opposite might be true.<br /> Then of curse the Technocracy has Technology i.e. Magic that is far beyond what is accepted by ordinary people.<br /> <br /> So to phrase it like you Technocrats aren't so much the might of the modern world distilled but are who build the modern world in the first place.<br /> <br /> Other examples for a high level Technocracy spells might be:<br /> one that tanks the economy of an entire country, to outsiders the casting of that spell might just look like someone working on his computer with banking/financial software for hours or days.<br /> <br /> A boardroom meeting where decisions are made and papers are signed etc. might be the ritual of a spell to build a planed neighbourhood or a factory etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T08:16:59-07:00","id":1333669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1332240-technocracy-how-do-truly-powerful-technocrats-look-like?p=1333525#post1333525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pjo is Percy Jackson.<br /> <br /> In other words, powerful technocrats are the might of the modern world, distilled and perfected to godlike levels. Just as a caveman would view airstrikes, cars, computers, and the internet as sorcery, so so modern humans view high powered technocrats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Technocracy are &quot;The New Gods&quot; if you've read American Gods or Seen the series. That is what high Level Technocrats should look like to the Olympians beings of modern and Alien pantheon. They might adapt its trappings but they will never be children of Technology or Media, or The Conspiracy. They are the Children of the Gods we worship every day but don't acknowledge(how often have you looked at your smartphone today? Would Ishtar have ever had such devotion?). They are frightening and powerful their miracles are the miracles of modernity taken to 11. IF they want to stop you from escaping traffic swells, your car breaks down or even a random act of violence occurs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T12:16:54-07:00","id":1334217,"title":"","content":"As an aside, my own idea of what Progenitor masters and arch masters (I'm blanking on most Union terminology at the moment) has always been influenced by SM Stirling's Draka books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-07T17:10:55-07:00","id":1334395,"title":"","content":"Ramnesis hit one of the key points I think, so to add to that: Technocrats think long term, and are patient and subtle. After all look at how they managed to shape Consensus successfully: they identified the key weakness, and started working towards that subtly and over time utilizing their leverage to nudge things their way. By the time the other mages realized what was happening, it was a done deal.<br /> <br /> So I think a powerful technocrat is going to be like that - alot of power, but power that is wielded subtly (coincidental or mundane), and potentially over a long term if they need to. It doesn't mean you wouldn't have supertech like rayguns or such.. it just wouldn't be obvious or it would be used in rare cases where consensus wasn't a problem. For example I could see a powerful Technocrat having something like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boeing_YAL-1\" target=\"_blank\">Airborne Laser</a> at their beck and call to blast anyone they needed blasting (conicidentally!) Or other versions (you can have vehicle mounted, or even something that is man/team portable - although we're still a long ways from small arms. Enough though to fit with 'coincidental' magic.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}